{
  "summary": "Use separate compact block nonces per network interface or bind address rather than a single shared nonce across all peers. Cached compact block representations (`CBlockHeaderAndShortTxIDs`) and their serializations are now constructed lazily per network key instead of eagerly upfront.",
  "problem": "Nodes currently reuse a single compact block nonce across all peers when serving the latest tip block from cache. An adversary connecting over multiple network types (such as IPv4 and Tor) can request the tip via `getdata(MSG_CMPCT_BLOCK)` and compare nonces to deanonymize and link the node's identities.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description explains the deanonymization vector: \"anyone can request the most recent tip as a compact block via `getdata(MSG_CMPCT_BLOCK)` over a clearnet and a tor connection and then compare the nonces - if they match it's the same node.\"",
    "Author notes the issue was identified and reported by Core contributor ajtowns on IRC."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
