  "card": "Nodes currently serve the cached latest compact block using a single shared nonce across all peers, allowing an adversary connecting via different networks (e.g., clearnet and Tor) to deanonymize the node by matching nonces in `MSG_CMPCT_BLOCK` responses. This change isolates compact block nonces per network key (`CNode::m_network_key`) and constructs compact block instances lazily per network. The deanonymization flaw was originally identified by ajtowns on IRC.",
